<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24869" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Īphĭtus</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἴφιτος.</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The son of Eurytus and Antiope</i>, <i>one of the Argonauts</i>, <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				14</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A Trojan</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 2,
				435</span></i>. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Īphĭtĭdes</span></b> ,
			ae, m., <i>son of
			Iphitus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Coeranos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 13, 257</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A king in Elis</i>, <i>who reinstated
				the Olympic games</i>, <i><span class="en">Val. Fl. 1, 363</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>